hi there are you as passionate about  programming as we are  if yes you are going to love our list of  the five top movies that capture this  high-tech exhilarating world stunningly  taking us vividly through the  significance of programming to the sheer  wonder of ai these hollywood  representations are a real must watch  for every programmer or budding  enthusiast  so let's dive right in happy watching  the first on our list is the pirates of  silicon valley a must for all  programming enthusiasts and also an  inspiration for startups and  entrepreneurs around the world it was  directed by martin burke and released in  1999.  the film depicts several events that led  to the i.t and computer revolution watch  how giants like microsoft and apple  designed personal computers get an  insight into other key industry players  ibm and xerox what's particularly  interesting is the depicted computing  wars between apple and microsoft right  from their beginnings the competition at  the time and the success of each  the main plot revolves around how steve  jobs the founder of apple and bill gates  the founder of microsoft ideated  brilliantly the creation of a personal  computer that everyone could benefit  from and how after a long tussle the two  firms finally announced their alliance  in 1997 to build a better world for  technology  thus if you're keen to learn how  personal computers were first developed  this movie is something you'll  absolutely love  next up we have antitrust which was  released in 2001 it is a techno thriller  film did you know that the world of  software also has its own dirty side  dive right into unravel as this is quite  an interesting take on the world you're  enthusiastic about the plot starts with  the ideal setup programmers working in a  corporation that not just pays well but  also offers a good working environment  a young talent a passionate programmer  gets the job in this organization only  to find out later of the wrong doings  that were being committed  this is where things start getting  attention grabbing the programmer goes  on to use his unique tech skills and  gets right to the bottom of it all  this movie is really an all-time  favorite for programmers globally as it  depicts the best ways of applying one's  sophisticated know-how in this domain it  hence still remains one of the best  programming movies of all time number  three on our list is jobs which was  released in 2013. it is a biographical  drama the film is based on the life of  steve jobs right from his school life  until the invention of the ipod the  movie of course depicts the success  story of jobs but it touches on some of  the more tangible inspiring elements  highlighting the way he worked the  creativity he put in and the game  changing mission that he had which  eventually changed the world the plot  revolves around creating and building  the apple company and the brand the  introduction of the iconic iphone which  went on to become the highest selling  product in the century the recreation of  the ipod launch scene that will  definitely leave you with goosebumps  ashton kutcher's portrayal of steve jobs  that was just phenomenal all in all the  story behind how apple became the  business enterprise it is today yes jobs  is one of the most motivating films for  people who have real ambitions and  dreams and who want to create a world of  success for themselves second on the  list is the imitation game if you love  working with numbers or algorithms this  one is especially an absolute treat for  you in fact all programmers may find the  film extremely engaging it came out in  2014 and revolves around the invention  of the world's very first computer by  alan turing and his team the imitation  game is historical drama based on the  life of the genius british mathematician  alan shuring who played an essential  role as a crypto analyst in deciphering  the enigma machine an encryption device  used by the nazis during the world war  ii to transmit code messages the sheer  fact that he imagined a computing  machine when people had no idea about  anything even close to it is absolutely  incredible he solved a problem that the  most talented and revealed could never  have in this way and the movie captures  the excitement of it all what's more  historians actually estimate that  breaking enigma shortened the war by two  plus years  saving over 14 million lives turing's  work inspired generations of research  into what scientists call sharing  machines today we call them computers  the topmost however on the list is the  social network the movie was released in  2010 it is a biographical drama and has  won the oscars for best adapted  screenplay best film editing and best  original score the film captures the  lives of mark zuckerberg and his friend  eduardo saverin showcasing them in  harvard university and the story behind  the most successful social media  platform ever seen facebook the movie  depicts that in 2003 harvard computer  sciences sophomore mark zuckerberg  launched a website called face smash  that would determine the attractiveness  of female students against one another  the site became an overnight sensation  among harvard students but stirred  controversies due to violations of the  harvard computer and privacy policies  subsequently it had to be brought down  despite its popularity this spurred  another innovation from zuckerberg and  his close friend sabrin and outlaunched  the facebook in early 2004 which as we  all now know went on to become the  world's biggest social networking site  facebook thus the plot takes you through  how facebook grew as a business giving  us interesting glimpses into the various  ups and downs along its way what's  unique is that even in a movie such as  this you would find yourself connecting  to what each of the characters feel as  their emotions have been depicted in the  most real-life manner there is no real  villain it's about the things that real  people do in real life to achieve  success like how one may commit  something immoral or screw over their  friends to get ahead of themselves  this film also makes you remember where  and why you started also confirming the  sheet heights a dedicated programmer can  really go on to achieve once capitalized  on their potential we hope you've  enjoyed this video the list doesn't end  here there are many other programming  movies that we think are good choices to  satisfy the programmer in you therefore  do let us know which movie you think we  have missed on our list and your  personal favorite on our list as well  all these programming movies are fun to  watch but at the same time our  information is well thanks for watching  and stay tuned for more from simplylearn  hi there if you like this video  subscribe to the simplylearn youtube  channel and click here to watch similar  videos turn it up and get certified  click here
 

